            <ArticleTitle>Noninvasive diagnosis of coronary artery disease in women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiovascular disease is the leading cause of mortality and significant morbidly among women in the United States. The frequent absence of antecedent symptoms, the potential for an initial fatal cardiac event and the limitations of currently available noninvasive diagnostic tests pose challenges to healthcare practitioners as they try to optimally risk stratify patients. Therefore, the purpose of this article is to discuss the accuracy of noninvasive tests for CAD diagnosis in women.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
